        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Can you give me feedback on how the plugin was written, are there things I missed or did wrong?\r\n\r\nFrom the general plugin developing point of view? I can't see anything particularly bad. Maybe something like:\r\n- I wouldn't create a `<C-q>` global Terminal mode mapping. This feels out of place here.\r\n- I'd probably not export the `state` table directly in favor of `get` function(s) that return copy of locally tracked state data.\r\n- The `config.win` might benefit from being a generic floating window config without dedicated set of fields (which can only be beneficial if not included fields are \"harmful\" to left to configure to the user).\r\n\r\n    It can also be a callable that returns a window config: it is a more robust way to define a config because it can react to terminal resizing. Which is also a good reminder: if there are persistent floating windows, there should be a `VimResized` autocommand (either one global or created temporarily while window is visible) that recomputes window config.\r\n\r\nHope this helps.",
            "created_at": "2025-09-13T18:13:36Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2004#issuecomment-3288698592",
            "id": 3288698592,
